	<section_number>45.2-515</section_number>
	<catch_line> Board of Coal Mining Examiners; purpose</catch_line>
	<text>
		The Board of Coal Mining Examiners (the Board) is established as a policy board in the executive branch of state government. The purpose of the Board is to issue certificates authorizing the performance of certain tasks.
	</text>
	<history>Code 1950, §§ 45-1 through 45-3; 1954, c. 191; 1966, c. 594, § 45.1-3; 1984, c. 590; 1994, c. 28, § 45.1-161.15; 2021, Sp. Sess. I, c. 387.</history>
